          "final_text_tail": "All 67 tests pass and the shell completion `cleanup_timeout` syncs correctly from `ctx_args`.\n\nThe implementation is complete. Summary of changes:\n\n**`src/click/core.py`**:\n- Added `import logging` and `import signal`.\n- Added module-level `_logger = logging.getLogger(\"click\")`.\n- Added `cleanup_timeout: float | None = None` parameter to `Context.__init__`.\n- Added validation: raises `ValueError` for zero, negative, or non-numeric values; `None` means no timeout; stored as a float.\n- Modified `close()` to run cleanup through `_close_with_timeout()` when a timeout is set.\n- Added `_close_with_timeout()` using `signal.SIGALRM` + `signal.setitimer` to forcibly terminate cleanup that exceeds the timeout, with a `TimeoutError` handler that logs a warning and degrades gracefully. Falls back to plain `close()` on platforms without `SIGALRM`.\n\n**`src/click/shell_completion.py`**:\n- `shell_complete()` now extracts `cleanup_timeout` from `ctx_args` and passes it to the completion class.\n- `ShellComplete.__init__` accepts `cleanup_timeout`, syncs it with `ctx_args`, and stores it.\n- `get_completions()` now closes the resolved context in a `finally` block so cleanup callbacks run (respecting `cleanup_timeout`).\n\nAll existing tests pass (148 across the relevant test files), and the new feature is verified functionally: positive floats work, `None` is the default, invalid values raise `ValueError`, and hanging cleanups are forcibly terminated after the timeout.",
